<Placemark>
<name>P01 · Slutsk</name>
<description><b>P01 · Slutsk</b><br/>Today: Slutsk, Minsk Region, Belarus<br/>Confidence: [C] · precision: town<br/>Jurisdictions: Russian Empire (Minsk gubernia) → Byelorussian SSR → Belarus (1991)<br/><br/><b>People &amp; events</b><br/>B02 lived with Israel's family (Sadovaya St., corner of the bedroom) `tania-project (§4)`<br/>B04 residence 1905–24, haberdashery shop, left Dec 1924/25 `tania-project (§§4, 28)`<br/>C06 b. 1880, seamstress, res. to Nov 1928 `tania-project (§35)`<br/>`EV-04`<br/>B10 b. 1909, school `tania-project (§35)`<br/>B11 b. Jun 1911, school + Bund `tania-project (§35)`<br/>Narrative, p. 14<br/>B12/B13/B14 b. 1914/17/21 `tania-project (§35)`<br/>B26 d. ~1921 `tania-project (§7)`<br/>C02 d. 1922 `EV-05`<br/>C03 res. (outskirts, at Ostrov) `Tanya-summary, p. 3`<br/>C04 d. 1895 `EV-25`<br/>C05 d. 1912 `EV-26`<br/>C07 2nd-grade teacher `tania-project (§16)`<br/>C08 head sexton of the Kalter shul `Slutsk Links, pp. 3–4`<br/>C09 d. 1919 `EV-33`<br/>C14 grain shop `tania-project (§32)`<br/>C15 pharmacist (Gipchin's), 1941 family suicide `tania-project (§33)`<br/>C16 d. 1915 `EV-44`<br/>X01 buried 5 Feb 1922, martyrs' row `EV-06`<br/>X02 d. 1915 `EV-52`<br/>X03 d. 1916 `EV-07`<br/>X04/X05 grew up in the Mostkoff home `tania-project (§3)`<br/>X18 Bolotnaya St. hides workshop `tania-project (§34)`<br/><br/><i>The corpus's center of gravity; the whole pinkas (EV-50) is the Slutsk Chevra Kadisha register. Micro-locations (kept here, not separate points): **Sadovaya Street** (Wolfson's courtyard, near the new synagogue, ~20–40 m from the Sluch river) `tania-project (§§2–3)`; **Proletarskaya Street** (the 1924 departure cart) `tania-project (§28)`; the **Sluch river**; the Kalter shul; Gipchin's pharmacy.</i><br/><br/><i>coords: 53.0275, 27.5528 — Wikidata Q201243 · GeoNames 621741; corroborated `tania-project (locations)`</i></description>
<Point><coordinates>27.5528,53.0275,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>P02 · Ostrov (near Slutsk)</name>
<description><b>P02 · Ostrov (near Slutsk)</b><br/>Today: village/outskirts near Slutsk, Minsk Region, Belarus — exact settlement unidentified<br/>Confidence: [?] · precision: approximate<br/>Jurisdictions: as Slutsk<br/><br/><b>People &amp; events</b><br/>B04 b. 1880 "in the shtetl of Ostrov" `tania-project (§§4, 35)`<br/>`MOSTKOFF, p. 1`<br/>C03 + C02 lived on the outskirts of Ostrov near Slutsk `Tanya-summary, p. 3`<br/><br/><i>**Disambiguation:** this is *not* Ostrów Mazowiecka or any Polish Ostrov — the corpus itself fixes it next to Slutsk ("Lived on the outskirts of Ostrov near Slutsk"; a Slutsk-pinkas Borukhovich is "Ostrever"). Wikidata has no Ostrov in Slutsk raion; the memoir site marks it approximate. Pin down via JewishGen Gazetteer / 19th-c. lists when possible.</i><br/><br/><i>coords: 53.0, 27.5 — `tania-project (locations)`, approximate</i></description>
<Point><coordinates>27.5,53.0,0</coordinates></Point>
</Placemark>
<Placemark>
<name>P03 · Nesvizh</name>
<description><b>P03 · Nesvizh</b><br/>Today: Niasviž, Minsk Region, Belarus<br/>Confidence: [C] · precision: town<br/>Jurisdictions: Russian Empire (Minsk gubernia) → Poland 1921–39 (Riga border ran just west of town — why the memoir says "near the Polish border") → Byelorussian SSR → Belarus<br/><br/><b>People &amp; events</b><br/>B02 Chaya — natal village region ("lived her whole life in a distant village near the Polish border, near Nesvizh")<br/>presumably died/buried there (CF-17 strong negative: not in the Slutsk register) `tania-project (§4)`<br/>Zaturensky revision-list lead (EV-36, EV-10)<br/><br/><i>The natal *village* itself is unidentified — a place to search (Nesvizh-area revision lists). See `docs/investigations/sapotnitsky.md`.</i><br/><br/><i>coords: 53.2189, 26.6819 — Wikidata Q201230 · GeoNames 624700; corroborated `tania-project (locations)` 53.22/26.69</i></description>
<Point><coordinates>26.6819,53.2189,0</coordinates></Point>
